From ba5b2950c036cb539216f79a9758e02da0a62dd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:28:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] drm/connector: Add the HDMI "Dolby Vision" property

In standard (TV-led) Dolby Vision the frames carry the Dolby Vision
signal, the video and its metadata, tunnelled in 8-bit RGB, and the sink
does the display mapping. User-space can make those frames, but has no
way to send the infoframe that tells the sink to decode them: without
it the sink shows them as SDR RGB.

Add an enum connector property, "Dolby Vision", in the connector's HDMI
state: "Off", or standard Dolby Vision signalled with the HDMI
vendor-specific infoframe padded to 24 bytes ("Standard (HDMI VSIF)"),
or with the Dolby one ("Standard (Dolby VSIF)"). Sinks with a version 2
Dolby Vision VSVDB are commonly sent the Dolby one, others the HDMI one;
the EDID block is left to user-space.

Low-latency (source-led) Dolby Vision is left out: there the source does
the display mapping, which needs more than infoframes.

The HDMI state helper implements the property in the next patch.
---
